## Universal vs Cell-Specific Terms (F13-ratified chat 2026-09-19, post-second-witness)

> **Status:** Documentation-consistency correction following the 2026-09-19 prompt-compartment audit.

The static audit's "cross-compartment leak" report treated `F13`, `SOVEREIGN`, and similar terms as A2H leakage when found in A2M prompts. This is an internal classification contradiction — those terms are universal constitutional references that predate the compartment doctrine.

**Universal terms** (may appear in any compartment without violating it):

- F1–F13 constitutional floors
- APEX-ZEN governance chain (`BUILD → VERIFY → JUDGE → SEAL → ACT → WITNESS`)
- `capability ≠ authority` invariant
- F13 SOVEREIGN (human-authority reference, cross-cutting)
- Identity, citizenship, FI ID
- Canonical-fragments pointer (`/root/AAA/instructions/`)
- APEX doctrine references

These appear in prompts of any compartment by design — they encode the constitutional floor system, not cell-specific content. Reclassification removes predictable false positives from keyword audits.

This is a documentation-consistency correction, not a security control. Lexical classification remains a heuristic; only the kernel reference monitor can determine actual privilege boundaries.

